# T1 Fan Site — CN Project 2

A fan website for T1, the League of Legends esports team, built for Computer Networking (Spring 2026).  
This project demonstrates real-world networking concepts including DNS, HTTPS, IP addressing, performance optimization, and network monitoring.

**Live Site:** https://thien1114.github.io/cn-project/

---

## Project Features

### Security (Mandatory)
- **HTTPS enforced** via GitHub Pages (automatic SSL/TLS certificate from Let's Encrypt). All HTTP requests are redirected to HTTPS.
- **XSS Protection** via [DOMPurify](https://github.com/cure53/DOMPurify) — all dynamic HTML is sanitized before being injected into the DOM.
- **Content Security Policy** meta tag restricts which scripts and resources the browser is allowed to load.

### Performance Optimization
- **Lazy loading** on all images using the `loading="lazy"` HTML attribute — images only load when they scroll into view.
- **Minified CSS** — production stylesheet is minified to reduce file size and page load time.
- **CDN delivery** — GitHub Pages serves assets through the Fastly CDN (via anycast routing), reducing latency for global users.

### Network Monitoring
- **Google Analytics** integrated to track page views, session duration, and user behavior over time.

---

## How to Run Locally

1. Clone the repository:
   ```
   git clone https://github.com/thien1114/cn-project.git
   ```
2. Open the project folder:
   ```
   cd cn-project
   ```
3. Open `index.html` in your browser directly, or use a local server:
   ```
   npx serve .
   ```
   Then visit `http://localhost:3000`

> No build step required. The site is plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

---

## File Structure

```
cn-project/
├── index.html        # Main HTML entry point
├── app.js            # All page logic and rendering
├── style.css         # Stylesheet
├── purify.min.js     # DOMPurify XSS sanitization library
├── images/           # Screenshots and site images
└── README.md         # This file
```

---

## Deployment (GitHub Pages)

1. Push changes to the `master` branch.
2. Go to **Settings → Pages** in the GitHub repository.
3. Set source to `master` branch, root folder.
4. Enable **Enforce HTTPS** checkbox.
5. GitHub Pages will automatically build and deploy the site within a few minutes.

The site is live at: `https://thien1114.github.io/cn-project/`

